// symbolon: the Linux command-line agent and its services.
//
//   symbolon relay serve DIR PORT [--tls CERT KEY] [--bind ADDR] [--ca FILE] [--store SPEC] [--store-ca FILE]
//       the sync service (SPEC 20.1, 29.4, 29.9); --console-origin https://HOST:PORT serves the console (29.10); --name HOST:PORT[,...]: the names devices reach the relay at, bound into their sign-in (29.4),
//       required (or --console-origin) unless --insecure-any-name takes any name a device signs; --store: a directory (DIR by default),
//       postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DB, s3://KEY:SECRET@HOST:PORT/BUCKET?region=R, or @FILE holding one;
//       --allow-private-witnesses: call witnesses at loopback, private or link-local addresses (tests);
//       --allow-witness HOST:PORT[,...]: call those of them only (a household box's own witnesses)
//   symbolon witness keygen KEYFILE            a witness's signing key; prints its public key
//   symbolon relay scim-token DIR ORG-ID          a bearer token for ORG-ID's SCIM directory (SPEC 29.7)
//   symbolon witness serve DIR PORT KEYFILE [OFFSET] [--tls CERT KEY] [--bind ADDR]
//                                              a witness (SPEC 20.3); OFFSET seconds added to its
//                                              clock (tests: time passing)
//       --tls: serve HTTPS with the PEM certificate chain CERT and private key KEY;
//       --bind: the address to listen on (default 127.0.0.1)
//   symbolon cosigner new DIR RELAY_HOST RELAY_PORT [--ca CA.pem]   prints the cosigner's keys
//   symbolon cosigner pair DIR DEVICE_KEYS              pins the device that runs the inception
//   symbolon cosigner serve DIR [PRIMES]
//   symbolon cosigner scan-leaks DIR           checks the mailbox for key material an old build exposed (SPEC 6.2.1)
//   symbolon device new DIR RELAY_HOST RELAY_PORT [--unprotected] [--fast-kdf] [--ca CA.pem]
//       --ca: speak TLS to the relay and the witnesses, trusting the PEM anchor CA.pem
//                                              PIN and duress PIN on stdin; prints the device's keys
//   symbolon device init DIR COSIGNER_KEYS W1 W2 W3 [DEVICE_PRIMES KIT_PRIMES]
//                                              W as host:port:keyhex; PIN on stdin, then the kit's
//                                              passphrase twice (an empty line: none; SPEC 13.2)
//   symbolon device register DIR RP [--duress] PIN on stdin; prints a credential ID and public key;
//                                              --duress puts it in the duress subset
//   symbolon device sign DIR RP CID MESSAGE    PIN on stdin; prints r || s
//   symbolon device status DIR                 "security-update due" while the update below has not run
//   symbolon device scan-leaks DIR             PIN on stdin; checks the mailbox for key material an old
//                                              build exposed (SPEC 6.2.1); exit 3 when it found some
//   symbolon device security-update DIR [PRIMES]  PIN, then the duress PIN (empty: none), on stdin; the duress
//                                              profile gets its own transport key, the device a new one (D-4)
//                                              then, once per household, the key refresh after the Paillier
//                                              nonce fix: a re-share with the cosigner and every other device
//                                              (src/agent/migrate.resid); status says "security-reshare STATE"
//   symbolon device security-advice DIR [--report lost|cosigner]   what to do after the nonce fix, in words
//                                              (replace the master key; rollover or each site's recovery);
//                                              --report: a device was lost or stolen, or the cosigner's
//                                              operator reported an incident (kept; the advice gets stricter)
//   symbolon device forget DIR
//   symbolon device vault login DIR NAME ORIGIN USERNAME     (PIN, password on stdin)
//   symbolon device rotate DIR NAME BUNDLE REPOSITORY [CHROMIUM] [--share ID]   (PIN on stdin)
//   symbolon device vault put DIR NAME         PIN then the secret on stdin
//   symbolon device vault get DIR NAME         PIN on stdin; prints the secret
//   symbolon device vault list DIR [--kinds|--long]  PIN on stdin; prints the names (--kinds: TYPE NAME;
//                                              --long: TYPE NAME-HEX DETAIL-HEX FOLDER-HEX [APPS-HEX]); offline, this device's copy
//   symbolon device vault breach DIR           PIN on stdin; each login's password against Pwned Passwords
//                                              (k-anonymity range query, SPEC 26.1): "breached NAME-HEX COUNT"
//                                              lines, "protected N not checked" if any,
//                                              then "checked N breached M"; SYMBOLON_BREACH_URL, _CA
//   symbolon device vault show DIR NAME        PIN on stdin; prints "FIELD VALUE-HEX" per field
//   symbolon device vault code DIR NAME        PIN on stdin; prints "code CODE PERIOD LEFT", the
//                                              item's current one-time code (its key never leaves)
//   symbolon device vault set DIR NAME TYPE    PIN, then "FIELD VALUE-HEX" lines, on stdin (card, identity,
//                                              note, bank, wifi, secret, login)
//   symbolon device vault delete DIR NAME      PIN on stdin
//   symbolon device vault import DIR FILE [--format auto|bitwarden-json|csv|1password-op] [--dry-run]
//       FILE "-": the export as one line on stdin, then the PIN
//   symbolon device vault signin-bitwarden DIR SERVER [--dry-run] [--share ID]
//       signs in to Bitwarden or Vaultwarden (SERVER: bitwarden.com,
//       bitwarden.eu or https://...) and imports the vault; a line
//       conversation on stdin/stdout (src/agent/bwsignin.resid)
//   symbolon device beacon DIR [--location LAT,LON,ACC,AGE]   (PIN; SPEC 14.4)
//   symbolon device alerts DIR | alerts set|register DIR | alerts inbox DIR
//   symbolon device duress end DIR                (PIN; src/agent/alertscli.resid)
//   symbolon home alerts DIR [set KEY VALUE]      the box's alert channels
//   symbolon device vault signin-lastpass DIR [--dry-run] [--share ID]
//       the same for LastPass, experimental (src/agent/lpsignin.resid)
//                                              PIN on stdin (not with --dry-run): another password
//                                              manager's export, as one new vault version
//   symbolon device openings DIR                  PIN on stdin; each device's protected-item openings (hour, day, week) from the cosigner's records, and whether a day is unusual
//   symbolon device protection enable DIR [PRIMES]  PIN on stdin; a re-share that gives the quorum a vault OPRF key (protected items, SPEC 18.10)
//   symbolon device vault protect DIR NAME   PIN on stdin; the item into the protected tier (SPEC 18.10): opening it then needs the cosigner
//   symbolon device vault unprotect DIR NAME PIN on stdin; back to the standard tier
//   symbolon device vault move DIR NAME TO [--unprotect]  PIN on stdin; to the own vault (TO "own") or the shared folder TO (a protected item only with --unprotect)
//       list, show, code, set, delete, import and move take a last `--share ID`: in (from) that shared folder
//   symbolon device share new DIR NAME         PIN on stdin; a shared folder (SPEC 19); prints its ID
//   symbolon device share list DIR             PIN on stdin; "ID NAME-HEX owner|member PEOPLE" per folder
//                                              ("ID - waiting WHY-HEX": no key for this device yet)
//   symbolon device share members DIR ID       PIN on stdin; "LOG-ID NAME-HEX FINGERPRINT owner|member"
//   symbolon device share add DIR ID LOG-ID NAME   PIN on stdin; the owner adds a person
//   symbolon device share remove DIR ID LOG-ID PIN on stdin; the owner removes a person (new key)
//   symbolon device share delete DIR ID        PIN on stdin; the owner deletes the folder
//   symbolon device share leave DIR ID         PIN on stdin; a member leaves (the owner's device then re-keys)
//   symbolon device share duress DIR ID on|off PIN on stdin; read the folder under the duress PIN on this device
//   symbolon device share card DIR NAME        PIN on stdin; the name others see; prints LOG-ID FINGERPRINT
//   symbolon device org new|join|show|members|add|remove|role|policy|group|groups|folder|sync|audit ...
//                                              organizations (SPEC 29); see src/agent/orgcli.resid
//   symbolon device share me DIR               prints LOG-ID FINGERPRINT
//   symbolon device share people DIR           "LOG-ID NAME-HEX FINGERPRINT me|-" per card at the relay
//   symbolon ssh-agent DIR [SOCKET]            the SSH agent (SPEC 16.1) on a Unix socket
//   symbolon ssh-agent-stdio DIR RUNDIR PEER   one agent connection on stdin/stdout (Android's service, SPEC 16.1.1)
//   symbolon device ssh new|import|list|sign|delete ...   SSH keys in the vault (src/agent/sshcli.resid)
//   symbolon device ssh ca-new|cas|certify|renew|certs|refresh ...   the SSH certificate authority (SPEC 16.1.2)
//   symbolon device link-new DIR [--host H,...] [...]   a new device: shows a code (QR) for an existing one (SPEC 11.5)
//   symbolon device link-add DIR               adds the device whose code was scanned (stdin: the link, the PIN, y)
//   symbolon device key add|list|remove DIR [NAME]   security keys as a second factor (SPEC 9.4)
//   symbolon device key fills DIR keys|any       PIN on stdin; whether fills need a security key (SPEC 22.7)
//       With SYMBOLON_FILL set (the fill window's request), vault list, show and code are a fill:
//       refused under "keys" with no key enrolled, and a key's touch signs over the request.
//   symbolon browser host [ORIGIN...]          the browser extension's native messaging host (SPEC 22.5);
//                                              SYMBOLON_CONSENT is the consent window (the app)
//   symbolon home init DIR HOST [HOST...] --witness H:P:KEY --witness H:P:KEY [--witness-ca FILE] [--ports BASE] [--bind ADDR]
//            [--seal tpm|passphrase] [--passphrase-file FILE]   Symbolon Home: the box's CA, certificates and witness,
//                                              keys sealed to the TPM or a passphrase; two witnesses outside the box
//   symbolon home secure DIR [--witness H:P:KEY ...] [seal flags]   an existing box: seals its keys, moves new people's witnesses off it
//   symbolon home status DIR                   JSON: sealed, witness majority off the box, the reminder
//   symbolon home witness-cert DIR HOST OUTDIR a TLS certificate under the box's CA for a witness outside it
//   symbolon home invite DIR NAME              a one-time code (a day) for NAME; prints the pairing link (QR)
//   symbolon device pin DIR                    PIN and the new PIN on stdin; changes the PIN
//   symbolon home serve DIR [--passphrase-file FILE] [--run DIR]   pairing, relay, the box's witness and every cosigner
//                                              (keys unsealed into DIR, a tmpfs, default /dev/shm)
//   symbolon device webauthn register DIR RP_ID [--uv] [--duress]          PIN on stdin; adds authenticator-data
//                                              and attestation-object (fmt none) to what register prints
//                                              --replaces CID: it replaces that imported (Synced) passkey
//   symbolon device webauthn retire DIR CID [--force]   PIN on stdin; deletes an imported passkey a
//                                              Symbolon passkey replaced (--force: any)
//   symbolon device webauthn assert DIR RP_ID CREDENTIAL_ID CDH [--uv]   PIN on stdin; authenticator-data,
//                                              signature-der, then r || s; a Synced passkey (imported)
//                                              prints "profile synced" and user-handle too
//   symbolon device webauthn synced DIR        PIN on stdin; the Synced passkeys an import brought:
//                                              "passkey CID RP USER USERNAME DISPLAY PUBLIC-KEY REPLACED-BY" (hex)
//   symbolon device enroll DIR NEW_KEYS [PRIMES]   PIN on stdin; adds the device NEW_KEYS (re-share)
//   symbolon device join DIR ENROLLER_KEYS [PRIMES] PIN on stdin; joins when that device enrolls this one
//   symbolon device recover DIR KIT LOG_ID    a new device starts a kit recovery (SPEC 13.2); stdin: the
//                                              kit's passphrase if it has one, then the new kit's twice
//   symbolon device veto DIR                   PIN on stdin; vetoes the latest pending event
//   symbolon device pending DIR                the log's pending events: SEQ KIND DIGEST, when each takes
//                                              effect, who signed it, whether it may be confirmed
//   symbolon device confirm DIR SEQ            stdin: the PIN, then y; this device confirms the pending
//                                              authority event SEQ another device signed: in force at once
//                                              (a confirm event, SPEC 8.2; never a recover or a weakening)
//   symbolon device kit-escape DIR KIT_SEED    the kit drops the log's sequencing relay (one that is gone or
//                                              refuses every claim): delayed by the recovery delay, vetoable (SPEC 20.3)
//   symbolon device sequence DIR [HOST:PORT]  PIN on stdin; names the relay (this device's, or HOST:PORT) as the
//                                              log's sequencer (policy field 8, SPEC 20.3): a set-policy
//   symbolon device witnesses DIR [--add HOST:PORT:KEY]... [--remove HOST:PORT]...   PIN on stdin; changes the
//                                              log's witnesses (SPEC 20.3): a set-policy, each added witness's
//                                              signed time checked first; delayed and vetoable unless signed by
//                                              policy[1] devices, and always when it removes one (SPEC 8.2)
//   symbolon device recover-release DIR        PIN on stdin; asks the cosigner for its kit half
//   symbolon device recover-finish DIR KIT [PRIMES]  PIN on stdin (then the kit's passphrase if it has one);
//                                              after the delay: release, re-share
//   symbolon device kit status DIR             whether the kit's sheet has a passphrase
//   symbolon device kit renew DIR [PRIMES]     replaces the kit (a lost or seen sheet, or to add a passphrase):
//                                              stdin: the PIN, then the new kit's passphrase twice (empty: none);
//                                              prints the new kit; a rotate-recovery (delayed and vetoable unless
//                                              policy[1] devices sign), then once in force a re-share to the new
//                                              kit (run it again after the delay); every old sheet is then dead
//
// Services listen on 127.0.0.1 only; put a TLS terminator in front of them
// for anything else (SPEC 20.2: envelopes are end to end, objects signed).

